# --- TARS environment ---
#
# Copy to .env for local development. Every value below is required for the
# deployed app to work, except where marked optional.
#
# Local setup start to finish, and the Vercel provisioning steps, are in
# docs/runbooks/deploy-vercel.md.

# --- Database (required) -----------------------------------------------------
# Postgres. SQLite is not an option on Vercel — serverless filesystems are
# ephemeral, so writes would be silently discarded between requests.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://tars:tars@127.0.0.1:5433/tars?schema=public"

# A separate database for the test suite. The suite refuses to run unless the
# name contains "_test", so a stray run cannot wipe development data.
TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://tars:tars@127.0.0.1:5433/tars_test?schema=public"

# --- Auth (required) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret. Generate one with: npx auth secret
AUTH_SECRET=""

# Google SSO, restricted to the @biome.in domain (see lib/auth.config.ts).
#
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Auth fails closed: with no provider configured nobody
# can sign in and the deployment is unreachable. That is deliberate for an app
# holding founder call transcripts, but it does mean these two are not optional.
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=""
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=""

# Local-only email + password sign-in, so a checkout with no OAuth credentials
# is still usable. Ignored when NODE_ENV=production, so setting it on Vercel by
# accident cannot open a password door. Seeded users share the password
# "tars-dev" (see prisma/seed.ts).
AUTH_DEV_CREDENTIALS="true"

# --- Roles (recommended) -----------------------------------------------------
# Who gets ADMIN. Comma-separated; case-insensitive. Everyone else who signs in
# with a @biome.in account becomes a PM, which can author the record but not
# manage users.
#
# Leaving this empty means nobody is an admin — a safer default than "first user
# wins", but it does mean you cannot change anyone's role from inside the app.
# Takes effect on the person's next sign-in.
ADMIN_EMAILS=""

# --- Extraction (optional; the only thing here that costs money) -------------
# Without a provider key, everything works except the "run extraction" step,
# which says so on the transcript page. Safe to leave empty until you want the
# machine to draft observations.
#
# Two providers are supported and the key you set decides which one runs.
# Gemini is the default: with GOOGLE_API_KEY set, extraction runs on Gemini
# even if the Anthropic key is also present. So deploying the Gemini key IS the
# cutover, and deleting it is the fallback — no code or config change either
# way. Cost table in docs/runbooks/deploy-vercel.md.
#
# Gemini (default). GOOGLE_API_KEY is read first, GEMINI_API_KEY second — the
# SDK's own precedence. Set one, not both.
#
# Enable billing on the Google project before the first production run. This is
# a data-governance requirement, not a throughput one: free-tier AI Studio
# prompts may be used for product improvement, and these prompts are founder
# call transcripts naming real people and discussing financials. The paid tier
# is what takes them out of that pool. (Rate limits are the secondary reason —
# tokens per minute binds, at roughly 78k input tokens per run.)
GOOGLE_API_KEY=""
# GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# Anthropic (the fallback path). Set this alone to run extraction on Claude.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# Optional. Overrides the model for whichever provider is active; unset falls
# back to that provider's pinned default — gemini-2.5-flash-lite on Gemini,
# claude-sonnet-5 on Anthropic (spec D6, amended 2026-07-30).
#
# Never pin a floating alias such as gemini-flash-latest: it re-points upstream
# and changes price and behaviour without a commit. If quality disappoints, the
# escalation order is gemini-2.5-flash, then gemini-3.1-flash-lite.
# EXTRACTION_MODEL="gemini-2.5-flash-lite"
#
# The two knobs below are Anthropic-only — the Gemini adapter ignores them and
# turns thinking off by its own family rule.
#
# How hard the model thinks while extracting. Defaults to "low", because the
# whole run has to finish inside one serverless function call (60s on Vercel's
# free tier) and a killed run produces nothing at all.
# EXTRACTION_EFFORT="medium"
#
# Whether the model thinks at all. Off by default: with thinking on, five of the
# six blocks on a real forty-minute transcript did not finish inside the block
# timeout. max_tokens caps thinking and output together, so on a long call the
# thinking competes with the drafts for the same budget — and the job itself is
# careful reading rather than reasoning (quote exactly, file against a row, tag
# an origin).
# EXTRACTION_THINKING="on"

# --- Fireflies (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# Lets a PM import a call transcript from Fireflies instead of pasting it. From
# Fireflies → Settings → Developer Settings → API key. Without it, the import
# control on the transcript page says it is off and naming this variable;
# pasting still works exactly as before.
#
# There is one Fireflies account for all of Biome, so this one key lists every
# call the company has ever recorded, and anyone signed in to TARS can pull the
# full transcript of any of them. Scoping cannot narrow it — every meeting has
# the same host — so treat adding this key as that decision.
#
# No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and do not add one. That prefix is the single path by
# which Next would inline the value into the browser bundle; the key is read on
# the server (lib/fireflies/client.ts) and only ever leaves as a yes/no.
FIREFLIES_API_KEY=""
